format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: inside-the-atom

lesson elements-and-the-periodic-table
title: Elements
minutes: 4
xp: 50
teaches: u1-atomic-number
teaches: u1-change-protons
relies_on: u1-particles

description:
    One number tells you which element an atom is: how many protons it has. You will build atoms and watch what happens to the element when you change that number.

cite ref-openstax-chem-ch2
supports: The number of protons (the atomic number) defines the element.

cite ref-iupac-table
supports: IUPAC publishes the periodic table of the elements (optional card).

card c01
kind: item
type: item
item: u1-l3-predict-gold-oxygen
scored: 0

card c02
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Protons tell you the element
figure: elements-by-protons
figure_at: 1

body:
    The number of [[proton|protons]] tells you which [[element]] an atom is. An atom with 6 protons is always carbon. 7 protons is always nitrogen. 8 protons is always oxygen.

card c03
kind: sim
type: atom-builder
scored: 0
task: This atom has 6 protons, so it is carbon. Add one proton and watch the element.
hint: Tap + once. 7 protons is nitrogen.

config:
    {
      "mode": "element",
      "goal": {
        "protons": 7
      },
      "start": {
        "protons": 6,
        "neutrons": 6,
        "electrons": 6
      },
      "lock": {
        "neutrons": true,
        "electrons": true
      },
      "maxProtons": 10,
      "objectives": [
        "u1-change-protons"
      ]
    }

card c04
kind: item
type: item
item: u1-l3-fill-six

card c05
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Change the protons, change the element
figure: change-protons
figure_at: 1

body:
    Add a proton and you get a different element. 6 protons is carbon, 7 is nitrogen and 8 is oxygen. The neutrons and electrons do not decide the element. The protons do.

card c06
kind: sim
type: atom-builder
scored: 0
task: Now this atom has 7 protons: nitrogen. Add one more to turn it into oxygen.
hint: Tap + once. 8 protons is oxygen.

config:
    {
      "mode": "element",
      "goal": {
        "protons": 8
      },
      "start": {
        "protons": 7,
        "neutrons": 7,
        "electrons": 7
      },
      "lock": {
        "neutrons": true,
        "electrons": true
      },
      "maxProtons": 10,
      "objectives": [
        "u1-change-protons"
      ]
    }

card c07
kind: item
type: item
item: u1-l3-tom-gain-proton

card c08
kind: item
type: item
item: u1-l3-choice-lose-proton

card c09
kind: item
type: item
item: u1-l3-choice-gold-oxygen

card c10
kind: teach
type: explain
tier: deeper
scored: 0
title: Go deeper: the periodic table
figure: table-cell
figure_at: 1

body:
    The [[periodic-table|periodic table]] lists every element in order of its number of protons. Each box shows that number, a short symbol and the name. You do not need to memorise it.
